\title{A limit order held inside UBI and sent only when the other side of the book reaches its price}
\description{
Nothing rests at the exchange, so the order is invisible until it is sent, and UBI estimates where it would have stood in the queue. The template must be a \code{limit} order with a price. With \code{paper} set, nothing is ever sent and the order is filled on paper from that estimate. UBI now runs every plain \code{limit} order with a price, \code{day} validity and no \code{synthetic} object as this type by default, so this class is needed only for \code{paper}. While it is held, its price and quantity are changed with \code{TradeableInstrument$modify_order(parent_id = ...)} and it is cancelled with \code{TradeableInstrument$cancel_parent()} or \code{cancel()}; once sent, it is changed by its broker order id like any other order. It answers HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed} and sends nothing to a broker until it fires, a price that is not a whole number of ticks is refused with HTTP 400 when it is placed, and a limit the market never reaches costs no order message at all, so keep the \code{parent_id} from the answer.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
